**src/billing.ts:24 · attempt 1 (accepted)**

The Stripe 2025-03-31 (basil) API change moved billing period tracking from the Subscription level to individual SubscriptionItem level, removing \`current_period_end\` from \`Stripe.Subscription\`. The guide specifies using a deterministic, non-throwing helper that calls \`reduce\` over \`s.items.data\` to find the max \`current_period_end\` across all items (returning 0 for empty items). The enclosing function context shows the helper \`subscriptionPeriodEnd\` already exists in the file (lines 4-6). The fix is to replace the direct property access \`event.data.object.current_period_end\` with a call to the existing \`subscriptionPeriodEnd(event.data.object)\` helper. Multi-item decision: using \`Math.max\` across all items' \`current_period_end\` values ensures correctness for both single-item subscriptions (same result as the old field) and multi-item subscriptions (returns the latest period end). No throws, nulls, or new failure modes are introduced; the existing \`return null\` branch is preserved unchanged.

