**src/billing.ts:18 · attempt 1 (accepted)**

The Stripe API version 2025-03-31.basil removed \`current_period_end\` from \`Stripe.Subscription\` and moved billing periods to the item level (\`Stripe.SubscriptionItem#current_period_end\`). 

The guide specifies a deterministic, non-throwing helper using \`reduce\` over \`s.items.data\` with \`Math.max\`, returning 0 for empty items. This helper is already present in the enclosing function context (lines 4-6), so I reuse it instead of adding a duplicate.

The fix replaces the direct \`subscription.current_period_end\` access at line 23 with a call to the existing \`subscriptionPeriodEnd(subscription)\` helper.

Multi-item decision: \`Math.max\` across all items' \`current_period_end\` values is used, which equals the single value for single-item subscriptions and returns the latest period end for multi-item subscriptions. This is consistent with the guide's prescribed approach.

Diagnostics: 2 → 1.

</details>

### Worth a look

- Runtime behavior was not checked; smoke-test billing and webhook responses against the target API version.
- No tests ran. Add coverage for the changed billing and webhook flows before merging.

### Decisions for you

- Confirm the latest-ending item is the desired billing rule: items ending \`[100, 200]\` → that item's \`{ start, end }\`; a single item is unchanged.
- Confirm what no items means (Stripe never returns that): the webhook keeps fetching the full subscription, API routes throw "subscription has no items". Check pagination: only returned \`items.data\` are considered.
- Coordinate the API-version rollout with dashboard webhook endpoints and other services.

